n / Indie </p> <a class="ai-overview" href="#ai" aria-label="View AI-use evidence for SLAM TANK: 3 of 8 areas"> <div class="ai-overview-head"> <span class="ai-overview-title"><span class="ai-overview-logo" aria-hidden="true">▶</span> AI USE <span class="muted">Developer disclosure scope</span></span> <span class="ai-overview-count"><strong>3</strong><span>/ 8</span></span> </div> <div class="ai-overview-grid"> <span class="ai-overview-tile" title="In-game generation：Explicitly stated no use"> <span class="ai-overview-symbol" aria-hidden="true">▣</span> <span class="ai-overview-name">In-game generation</span> </span><span class="ai-overview-tile is-used" title="Code：AI use disclosed"> <span class="ai-overview-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span> <span class="ai-overview-name">Code</span> </span><span class="ai-overview-tile is-used" title="Art：AI use disclosed"> <span class="ai-overview-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◈</span> <span class="ai-overview-name">Art</span> </span><span class="ai-overview-tile" title="Music &#38; sound：Not stated"> <span class="ai-overview-symbol" aria-hidden="true">♫</span> <span class="ai-overview-name">Music &amp; sound</span> </span><span class="ai-overview-tile" title="Voice：Not stated"> <span class="ai-overview-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◉</span> <span class="ai-overview-name">Voice</span> </span><span class="ai-overview-tile" title="Writing：Not stated"> <span class="ai-overview-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✎</span> <span class="ai-overview-name">Writing</span> </span><span class="ai-overview-tile" title="Translation：Not stated"> <span class="ai-overview-symbol" aria-hidden="true">文</span> <span class="ai-overview-name">Translation</span> </span><span class="ai-overview-tile is-used" title="Marketing：AI use disclosed"> <span class="ai-overview-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span> <span class="ai-overview-name">Marketing</span> </span> </div> <div class="ai-overview-foot"><span><i class="ai-key used"></i>Reported use</span><span><i class="ai-key"></i>Unmarked does not mean AI-free</span><span class="ai-overview-arrow">View evidence ↗</span></div> </a> <div class="ai-chips"> <span class="chip used">Code</span><span class="chip used">Art</span><span class="chip used">Marketing</span>  </div> <div class="actions"> <a class="btn primary" href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/5186030/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Steam store ↗</a> <button class="btn" id="saveBtn" type="button" title="Saved in this browser only">☆ Save</button> <button class="btn" id="shareBtn" type="button">Share</button> </div> <dl class="facts"> <div><dt>Steam App ID</dt><dd><code>5186030</code><button class="copy" id="copyId" type="button">Copy</button></dd></div> <div><dt>Developer</dt><dd>Next Stage Inc.</dd></div> <div><dt>Publisher</dt><dd>Next Stage Inc.</dd></div> <div><dt>Release date</dt><dd>To be announced（计划；核查时尚未发售）</dd></div> <div><dt>Price</dt><dd>Not confirmed</dd></div> <div><dt>Platforms</dt><dd>Windows</dd></div> <div><dt>Genres</dt><dd>Action / Indie</dd></div> <div><dt>Tags</dt><dd>单人、完全支持控制器、家庭共享</dd></div>   <div><dt>Languages</dt><dd class="clamp">英语, 韩语, 法语, 德语, 西班牙语 - 西班牙, 日语, 葡萄牙语 - 巴西, 俄语, 简体中文, 繁体中文, 乌克兰语</dd></div> <div><dt>Website</dt><dd><a href="https://nextstage.co.kr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">nextstage.co.kr ↗</a></dd></div>  </dl> </aside> </section> <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="On this page"> <a href="#ai">AI use</a> <a href="#evidence">Evidence</a> <a href="#steam">Steam data</a> <a href="#developer">Developer</a> <a href="#sources">Sources &amp; corrections</a> </nav> <section class="section" id="ai"> <div class="section-head"> <div><div class="eyebrow">AI USE</div><h2>Eight areas, separate answers</h2></div> <div class="section-meta">3 / 8 areas with reported AI use</div> </div> <div class="status-note tone-amber"> <strong>Official AI disclosure</strong><span>The developer has disclosed generative AI use. The original source defines its scope.</span> </div> <p class="section-lede">A single-player tank action game that swings its cannon like a fist. The developer states generative AI tools assisted programming tasks and were used to create or refine selected 3D models and selected Steam marketing artwork, all reviewed, edited and tested by the team, and states that the game does not generate content with AI during gameplay and does not connect to an external AI service.</p>  <div class="table-wrap"> <table class="ai-table"> <thead> <tr><th>Area</th><th>Scope</th><th>Status</th><th>Notes</th></tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>In-game generation</strong><small>In-game AI</small></td> <td class="muted">Content generated during play</td> <td><span class="state s-none">Explicitly stated no use</span></td> <td class="muted">The disclosure states the game does not generate content with AI during gameplay and does not connect to an external AI service.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Code</strong><small>Code</small><a href="#evidence" class="area-provenance">View source ↗</a></td> <td class="muted">Programming and development</td> <td><span class="state s-used">AI use disclosed</span></td> <td class="muted">The disclosure states AI-assisted tools helped with programming tasks and that the AI-assisted code was reviewed, edited and tested by the team.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Art</strong><small>Art</small><a href="#evidence" class="area-provenance">View source ↗</a></td> <td class="muted">Visual assets</td> <td><span class="state s-used">AI use disclosed</span></td> <td class="muted">Selected 3D models were created or refined with AI assistance and reviewed by the team.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Music &amp; sound</strong><small>Music &amp; SFX</small></td> <td class="muted">Music and sound</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Voice</strong><small>Voice</small></td> <td class="muted">Voice and dialogue audio</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Writing</strong><small>Writing</small></td> <td class="muted">Story and written content</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Translation</strong><small>Translation</small></td> <td class="muted">Translation and localization</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Marketing</strong><small>Marketing</small><a href="#evidence" class="area-provenance">View source ↗</a></td> <td class="muted">Promotional material</td> <td><span class="state s-used">AI use disclosed</span></td> <td class="muted">Selected Steam marketing artwork was produced with AI-assisted tools.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> <div class="legend"> <span><i class="dot used"></i>Reported use (official / third-party)</span> <span><i class="dot not_stated"></i>Not stated (not proof of no use)</span> <span><i class="dot claimed_none"></i>Developer claims no AI</span> <span><i class="dot unreviewed"></i>Unreviewed</span> </div> <blockquote class="quote"> <p>“Generative AI-assisted tools were used during development to assist with programming tasks and to create or refine selected 3D models. All AI-assisted code and 3D assets were reviewed, edited, tested, and integrated by the development team. AI-assisted tools were also used for selected Steam marketing artwork. The game does not generate content with AI during gameplay and does not connect to an external AI service.”</p> <footer>Steam 商店 AI 生成内容披露栏完整原文，2026-10-31 核查；可能随商店页更新。 · <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/5186030/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read original ↗</a></footer> </blockquote> <details class="callout"> <summary><strong>How to interpret these statuses</strong></summary> <p>Reported AI use: 3/8. Developer no-use claims: 0/8. Claims are not independent verification; not stated does not mean no AI use.</p> </details> <p class="source-line"> Primary source:<a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/5186030/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official disclosure ↗</a> <span> · Reviewed 2026-10-31</span> </p> </section> <section class="section" id="evidence"> <div class="section-head"> <div><div class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE</div><h2>Evidence</h2></div> <div class="section-meta">6 sources</div> </div> <div class="timeline"> <article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Official disclosure</span> <time>2026-10-31</time> </div> <h3>Steam 商店完整 AI 披露</h3> <p>Generative AI-assisted tools were used during development to assist with programming tasks and to create or refine selected 3D models. All AI-assisted code and 3D assets were reviewed, edited, tested, and integrated by the development team. AI-assisted tools were also used for selected Steam marketing artwork. The game does not generate content with AI during gameplay and does not connect to an external AI service.</p> <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/5186030/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Steam discussion index</span> <time>2026-10-31</time> </div> <h3>Steam 讨论区首页核查</h3> <p>英文讨论区首页显示 15 个主题（总数 86）；仅覆盖首页。</p> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Community report</span> <time>2026-10-31</time> </div> <h3>Everyone passing because AI</h3> <p>You will never play or buy a game again. AI is the future. Within 5 years entire games will be 100% made, developed and voiced by AI. People are already not buying anything with AI used in any capacity. Okay, never buy or play a game past 2023 then. SoulKing View Profile View Posts 2 1 1 1 1 Oct 20 @ 9:03am Report this post AI shillers be freaking hilarious they should do stand-up comedy lmao #1 Fear57 View Profile View Posts 3 Oct 20 @ 9:07am Report this post Fact buddy. Its here and its going nowhere. You are the person laughing at the clown on stage who is saying the building is on fire. Last edited by Fear57 ; Oct 20 @ 9:08am #2 thomzen View Profile View Posts Oct 20 @ 9:22am Report this post Originally posted by Fear57 : Fact buddy. Its here and its going nowhere. You are the person laughing at the clown on stage who is saying the building is on fire. Saying &quot;it is going nowhere&quot; is such a defeatist statement. Gamers have the power to choose what games they buy. If games developed with AI don&#39;t get any sales and &quot;regular&quot; games do then game developers will eventually stop using AI. In the end the consumer has the choice to vote with their wallet #3 Raulikien View Profile View Posts 1 1 Oct 20 @ 9:23am Report this post Originally posted by Thomzen : Originally posted by Fear57 : Fact buddy. Its here and its going nowhere. You are the person laughing at the clown on stage who is saying the building is on fire. Saying &quot;it is going nowhere&quot; is such a defeatist statement. Gamers have the power to choose what games they buy. If games developed with AI don&#39;t get any sales and &quot;regular&quot; games do then game developers will eventually stop using AI. In the end the consumer has the choice to vote with their wallet Do you tell developers to code in 0s and 1s instead of programming languages that make it easier to program? Are they dumb because they don&#39;t do it the &quot;true&quot; way? The same reaction happened when we invented phonograph (canned music!), cameras (painting is the only true art!), electricity, internet, cars... If humanity had waited for people like you to give them permission to innovate, the world would be so boring. Oh, and we&#39;ll all be dead by now without any technologies if we feared used them. All of them are dual use, we exploit the good, minimize the bad. AI coding and asset generation literally enables indie developers to do passion projects and what used to require millions of dollars and expensive dev teams. It literally democratizes art and access to infinite entertainment for everyone. You should be complaining about the low effort generic human slop that triple A companies do every year, instead of moaning about the golden age of gaming and modding that is coming thanks to new technologies. Last edited by Raulikien ; Oct 20 @ 9:28am #4 thomzen View Profile View Posts Oct 20 @ 9:26am Report this post Originally posted by Raulikien : Originally posted by Thomzen : Saying &quot;it is going nowhere&quot; is such a defeatist statement. Gamers have the power to choose what games they buy. If games developed with AI don&#39;t get any sales and &quot;regular&quot; games do then game developers will eventually stop using AI. In the end the consumer has the choice to vote with their wallet AI literally enables indie developers to do passion projects and what used to require millions of dollars and expensive dev teams. It literally democratizes art and access to infinite entertainment. You should be complaining about the low effort generic human slop that triple A companies do every year. This is also true. Both statements can be true at the same time #5 CatCatCatCatCat!!!! View Profile View Posts Oct 20 @ 2:35pm Report this post If AI is the future why are you so upset? #6 Gilver View Profile View Posts Oct 20 @ 4:35pm Report this post I dont mind AI when its used for programming but it makes visuals look like ♥♥♥♥ #7 Zeruca View Profile View Posts Oct 20 @ 7:58pm Report this post Originally posted by SoulKing : AI shillers be freaking hilarious they should do stand-up comedy lmao All the kids supporting AI were the same people supporting NFTs #8 DrBrogbo View Profile View Posts Oct 20 @ 10:20pm Report this post Originally posted by Fear57 : You will never play or buy a game again. AI is the future. Within 5 years entire games will be 100% made, developed and voiced by AI. People are already not buying anything with AI used in any capacity. Okay, never buy or play a game past 2023 then. Okay. #9 Ensign View Profile View Posts 1 Oct 21 @ 10:12am Report this post AI hate in ALL its forms is something we will have to get used to. Remember back in the day when people found out Carbs were bad and we had to advertise everything as low carb or carb free? Then we found out there were GOOD carbs so we went on to hate Trans Fats. Remember when we realized mouths were filled with germs and bacteria so mouthwash was advertised as killing 99.9% of all germs till we realized there were beneficial germs we were killing too so now its low or no alcohol in mouthwash. Violence in videogames is abhorant and disgusting according to late 80s early to mid 90s adults! Its the scourge of our youth! (before that it was gangs, before that it was drugs, before that it was rock and roll music) Then we learned to move on and hate profanity then anything sexual. Dont pay it too much mind. AI is used to make &quot;slop&quot;. But we must remember its a tool at the end of the day and has its uses. AI is the future. The world was in great turmoil when we lost generations of cultivating/smithing knowledge when the industrial revolution came and eliminated those jobs. But we are all better off even if it did affect MANY families and regular people. People are making things with AI that NEVER would have been made without it. Mods, Videos, music! People without the know how on how to do these things are doing it with AI. Without those people these things wouldnt have been made. As an example people are making entire shows about for example the Malfoid trend. A real person a real artist, a real writer woudlnt have taken on that project since no one would have funded it. But some guy did it with the help of AI and its excellent. #10 Discop View Profile View Posts Oct 21 @ 12:27pm Report this post I think it&#39;s great but I agree on the AI Art. A lot of it looks like slop that could be done a bit better. It all got that deep fry look that you get when you ask Chatgpt for multiple times to edit an image. #11 Kildan24 View Profile View Posts Oct 21 @ 1:49pm Report this post AI is not a tool. It is a cancer. It&#39;s not used to make labors of love, it&#39;s used to make the mediocre think they&#39;re gifted. It&#39;s for lazy people who want to make a quick buck. #12 Ensign View Profile View Posts 1 Oct 21 @ 1:58pm Report this post Originally posted by Kildan24 : AI is not a tool. It is a cancer. It&#39;s not used to make labors of love, it&#39;s used to make the mediocre think they&#39;re gifted. It&#39;s for lazy people who want to make a quick buck. You havent explored enough. There are many labors of love out here. Go play rimworld and you will find quite a few labor of love mods both quality of life and game changing from people like me who love the game but dont have the know how on how to make mods so they just &quot;vibe code&quot; thier own. Its not for profit, its for personal use and they share it with us incase anyone else wants to try it. Again on youtube there are people trying to make money yes, but amoung the sea of greedy mediocre drama ai audio reads and lazy history videos there is actual entertainment being made music that would never have been made, animations that never would have been made. It is absolutely a tool. #13 Geist View Profile View Posts 1 Oct 21 @ 2:33pm Report this post Gameplay is all that matters. #14 RamblyBear View Profile View Posts Oct 23 @ 2:51pm Report this post Originally posted by Fear57 : You will never play or buy a game again. AI is the future. Within 5 years entire games will be 100% made, developed and voiced by AI. People are already not buying anything with AI used in any capacity. Okay, never buy or play a game past 2023 then. Actually fun thing about free will, we can all choose for ourselves how much is too much AI or too little AI. In this case the game suffers because the music quality is terrible and you can hear how it breaks down. The cinematics suffer because the two second cuts show us that they couldn&#39;t even pay for a premium video making AI account. When we really can&#39;t tell, then much less people will care. But while its this obvious, no one wants to engage in media that doesn&#39;t have a soul. We all reserve the right to feel differently about it later. #15</p> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/0/568174730608300015/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Community report</span> <time>2026-10-31</time> </div> <h3>People will be blown away in a year or two, when big AI projects will begin to release.</h3> <p>Blown like never before. You will have so many games to choose from, and so cheap, that you&#39;ll wet your pants. The gaming industry will be flipped on its head. You will have 1000 more games than now in a few years. And there will be super unique and original stuff there also. Scyrenus View Profile View Posts 1 Oct 27 @ 12:48am Report this post Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality. AI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff. #1 ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ View Profile View Posts 1 1 Oct 27 @ 4:22am Report this post Originally posted by Scyrenus : Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality. AI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff. The neoluddite attitude will fade with time, newer generations will embrace the future which is AI, same thing happened with horse drawn carriages, they were eventually replaced by the combustion engine. Not using AI is vastly ineffecient. #2 Scyrenus View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 4:24am Report this post Originally posted by ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ : Originally posted by Scyrenus : Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality. AI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff. The neoluddite attitude will fade with time, newer generations will embrace the future which is AI, same thing happened with horse drawn carriages, they were eventually replaced by the combustion engine. Not using AI is vastly ineffecient. Sure, using AI as a tool is great to check grammar, reorganize spreadsheets, and to help with science, but keep it away from art with a thousand-mile-long pole. #3 ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 4:33am Report this post Originally posted by Scyrenus : Originally posted by ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ : The neoluddite attitude will fade with time, newer generations will embrace the future which is AI, same thing happened with horse drawn carriages, they were eventually replaced by the combustion engine. Not using AI is vastly ineffecient. Sure, using AI as a tool is great to check grammar, reorganize spreadsheets, and to help with science, but keep it away from art with a thousand-mile-long pole. People said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren&#39;t restricted by time and money. #4 Scyrenus View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 4:38am Report this post Originally posted by ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ : Originally posted by Scyrenus : Sure, using AI as a tool is great to check grammar, reorganize spreadsheets, and to help with science, but keep it away from art with a thousand-mile-long pole. People said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren&#39;t restricted by time and money. Sure, but it still takes skill, effort, and intent to create good photos using a camera or to create digital art. If all you care about is more content, then it is fine. Heck, I even play idle games to get that serotonin running in my brain from time to time, but in general I care more about how things are made and what the artist is trying to convey. Otherwise, content for the sake of content is simply bland, degrading slop. There is a reason why some newer artists are returning to older methods of mediums in music, movies, and video games, because people still crave that old authenticity that gives art meaning. #5 Poyzo View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 7:43am Report this post People rejected radio, TV, the Internet and now AI. They&#39;ll come to learn to accept it, or be left behind. Either way, AI IS the future. #6 diesoon View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 11:20am Report this post Originally posted by Scyrenus : Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality. AI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff. You will just abandon your backlog again because new mindblowing stuff made with AI will arrive, and you won&#39;t care, you will just enjoy. #7 Scyrenus View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 12:50pm Report this post Originally posted by diesoon : Originally posted by Scyrenus : Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality. AI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff. You will just abandon your backlog again because new mindblowing stuff made with AI will arrive, and you won&#39;t care, you will just enjoy. Knowing my snobby ahh, I absolutely doubt it. After all I do keep playing old games over and over again even now. + I will always care, I love watching and studying behind the scenes to see how stuff is made. #8 ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 7:15pm Report this post Originally posted by Scyrenus : Originally posted by ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ : People said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren&#39;t restricted by time and money. Sure, but it still takes skill, effort, and intent to create good photos using a camera or to create digital art. If all you care about is more content, then it is fine. Heck, I even play idle games to get that serotonin running in my brain from time to time, but in general I care more about how things are made and what the artist is trying to convey. Otherwise, content for the sake of content is simply bland, degrading slop. There is a reason why some newer artists are returning to older methods of mediums in music, movies, and video games, because people still crave that old authenticity that gives art meaning. Just because something takes a lot of time or effort to produce doesn&#39;t mean it will appeal to people, like carving figurines out of wood requires considerable time and effort, but it&#39;s not like there are a lot of people who would actually want to buy these wooden figurines. Most people would rather buy a mass-produced figurine molded by a machine in a factory. AI is just another tool exactly like the camera, that enables people to create their own envisioned games. If the end product is good then it doesn&#39;t matter if AI was involved or not. #9 Scyrenus View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 9:03pm Report this post Originally posted by ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ : Originally posted by Scyrenus : Sure, but it still takes skill, effort, and intent to create good photos using a camera or to create digital art. If all you care about is more content, then it is fine. Heck, I even play idle games to get that serotonin running in my brain from time to time, but in general I care more about how things are made and what the artist is trying to convey. Otherwise, content for the sake of content is simply bland, degrading slop. There is a reason why some newer artists are returning to older methods of mediums in music, movies, and video games, because people still crave that old authenticity that gives art meaning. Just because something takes a lot of time or effort to produce doesn&#39;t mean it will appeal to people, like carving figurines out of wood requires considerable time and effort, but it&#39;s not like there are a lot of people who would actually want to buy these wooden figurines. Most people would rather buy a mass-produced figurine molded by a machine in a factory. AI is just another tool exactly like the camera, that enables people to create their own envisioned games. If the end product is good then it doesn&#39;t matter if AI was involved or not. Ayyy, thanks, now I want to visit some artsy craftsy stores to start making figurines. Also, we&#39;re not talking about appeal here, people have always loved cheap slop even during pre-AI era. And I do agree that effort doesn&#39;t always pay off, but it does teach you a lot even if it is a failed endeavor. If it is made by AI the final product is only a product, it inherently cannot be considered good or bad, it simply exists with no value attached to it. Because why would I pay for something if the developers didn&#39;t bother putting a part of themselves into the project? #10 REDSHADOW View Profile View Posts Oct 29 @ 8:36am Report this post Thats something that a person who is depending on AI to succeed would say. You are not fooling me AI Simp! AI WILL NOT REPLACES US! Last edited by REDSHADOW ; 1 hour ago #11 Super Jelly View Profile View Posts 9 hours ago Report this post Originally posted by Scyrenus : Originally posted by ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ : People said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren&#39;t restricted by time and money. Sure, but it still takes skill, effort, and intent to create good photos using a camera or to create digital art. If all you care about is more content, then it is fine. Heck, I even play idle games to get that serotonin running in my brain from time to time, but in general I care more about how things are made and what the artist is trying to convey. Otherwise, content for the sake of content is simply bland, degrading slop. There is a reason why some newer artists are returning to older methods of mediums in music, movies, and video games, because people still crave that old authenticity that gives art meaning. What are you talking about? Taking a photo is just point and shoot. You just press a button. 😁 #12</p> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/0/568175240219519653/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Community report</span> <time>2026-10-31</time> </div> <h3>How are you gonna have an anti-AI plot and then use AI unironically?</h3> <p>Holy fail. Revanchist1ab View Profile View Posts Oct 28 @ 11:26pm Report this post It is pretty funny how the troop carriers are basically massive GPU holders. #1</p> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/0/568175240219511182/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Community report</span> <time>2026-10-31</time> </div> <h3>Was excited until i saw it was made by ai</h3> <p>The whole game was generated by ai… If you didn’t bother making it, I won’t bother consuming and paying for it Simple as that UndeadBulwark View Profile View Posts Oct 17 @ 5:02pm Report this post First that&#39;s not how AI assisted game development works, and honestly I am tired of seeing you guys like go find some other fake outrage to be angry about or actually care about the real issues like the debt bomb in the US economy built by the AI stack that is getting its ass beat by Chinese AI. #1 Qtael View Profile View Posts 5 Oct 17 @ 7:56pm Report this post Originally posted by UndeadBulwark : First that&#39;s not how AI assisted game development works, and honestly I am tired of seeing you guys like go find some other fake outrage to be angry about or actually care about the real issues like the debt bomb in the US economy built by the AI stack that is getting its ass beat by Chinese AI. not that deep buddy, i see AI i skip it, simple as that would never pay for lazy &quot;work&quot; #2 UndeadBulwark View Profile View Posts Oct 17 @ 11:39pm Report this post Originally posted by Qtael : Originally posted by UndeadBulwark : First that&#39;s not how AI assisted game development works, and honestly I am tired of seeing you guys like go find some other fake outrage to be angry about or actually care about the real issues like the debt bomb in the US economy built by the AI stack that is getting its ass beat by Chinese AI. not that deep buddy, i see AI i skip it, simple as that would never pay for lazy &quot;work&quot; You know what you&#39;re right you do you, #3 JiggleBill View Profile View Posts 1 Oct 18 @ 2:53pm Report this post Get ready to skip everything. May want to start looking for that patch of woods you&#39;ll be living in soon. Start collecting sticks to eat with. #4 Qtael View Profile View Posts 1 Oct 18 @ 4:11pm Report this post Originally posted by JiggleBill : Get ready to skip everything. May want to start looking for that patch of woods you&#39;ll be living in soon. Start collecting sticks to eat with. Calm down goofy #5 fenixblue View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 10:25am Report this post Originally posted by JiggleBill : Get ready to skip everything. May want to start looking for that patch of woods you&#39;ll be living in soon. Start collecting sticks to eat with. If the aisludge of slopfest is what&#39;s going to be skipped, nobody is going to bat an eye. #6 gluemchen|A place far far away View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 10:37am Report this post Also keep in mind they slop created this garbage by copying the original creators game &quot;Tank Fu&quot; on steam. Nasty people. I have no problem with AI, If it is done in a manner that benefits the actual developer. This game is the opposite. There are things such as copying great mechanics for a game and there is straight off ripping off by using AI to advantage to have an earlier release as the original creator. Nasty practice and should be condemned. #7 UndeadBulwark View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 10:59am Report this post Originally posted by gluemchen|A place far far away : Also keep in mind they slop created this garbage by copying the original creators game &quot;Tank Fu&quot; on steam. Nasty people. I have no problem with AI, If it is done in a manner that benefits the actual developer. This game is the opposite. There are things such as copying great mechanics for a game and there is straight off ripping off by using AI to advantage to have an earlier release as the original creator. Nasty practice and should be condemned. Tank fu is a different game and I am pretty sure I saw them also put the game in r/AIGameDev #8 Wayne_B View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 2:34pm Report this post Originally posted by Qtael : The whole game was generated by ai… If you didn’t bother making it, I won’t bother consuming and paying for it Simple as that im going to buy it now. #9 Qtael View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 6:36pm Report this post Originally posted by Wayne_B : Originally posted by Qtael : The whole game was generated by ai… If you didn’t bother making it, I won’t bother consuming and paying for it Simple as that im going to buy it now. You deserve it #10 ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 7:00pm Report this post Gonna buy it too, AI is the future, every game developer should use AI tools to vastly increase their own productivity. #11 UndeadBulwark View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 8:41pm Report this post Originally posted by ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ : Gonna buy it too, AI is the future, every game developer should use AI tools to vastly increase their own productivity. I tried AI Game Dev and holy ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ ♥♥♥♥ so much of the tedious stuff can be passed onto an AI its amazing and I am using a local model with 256k context. #12 Qtael View Profile View Posts Oct 28 @ 1:33am Report this post Originally posted by UndeadBulwark : Originally posted by ☢Paradoxic Gamer☢ : Gonna buy it too, AI is the future, every game developer should use AI tools to vastly increase their own productivity. I tried AI Game Dev and holy ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ ♥♥♥♥ so much of the tedious stuff can be passed onto an AI its amazing and I am using a local model with 256k context. Tediuos stuff is what makes the art amazing look at Wildwood, it took them 16 years to animate it with their hands, and it&#39;s the best stop motion movie i&#39;ve watched ever and it will become a classic Too many shortcuts lead to dry results #13 MJay624 View Profile View Posts Oct 28 @ 2:29am Report this post Originally posted by JiggleBill : Get ready to skip everything. May want to start looking for that patch of woods you&#39;ll be living in soon. Start collecting sticks to eat with. You DO realize a ton of gamers only play older games made before AI existed, right? That and tons of indie devs despise AI taking their jobs and ruining games. There will always be anti AI games made. True artists tend to hate AI devaluing their work. #14 UndeadBulwark View Profile View Posts Oct 28 @ 8:03am Report this post Originally posted by MJay624 : Originally posted by JiggleBill : Get ready to skip everything. May want to start looking for that patch of woods you&#39;ll be living in soon. Start collecting sticks to eat with. You DO realize a ton of gamers only play older games made before AI existed, right? That and tons of indie devs despise AI taking their jobs and ruining games. There will always be anti AI games made. True artists tend to hate AI devaluing their work. This is the exact same sh*t that was said about &quot;Real&quot; art and Digital art guess who won. Last edited by UndeadBulwark ; Oct 28 @ 8:03am #15</p> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/0/568174540165810821/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article> </div> <details class="callout"><summary><strong>Review notes (expand)</strong></summary><p>Reviewed the full English Steam AI disclosure, the identity (developer Next Stage Inc., self-published) and the English discussion homepage (15 visible topics of 86), where four topics directly concern AI use; all four threads were opened and read in full. This title was searched 1 time with 4 results and 0 raw source(s) were read: the related Reddit thread returned HTTP 403 to the relay and the remaining results were store pages and google.com/goto redirect shells. The forum threads are player criticism and argument about AI use and are logged without changing any area finding; the claim that the whole game was generated by AI does not match the store disclosure, which limits AI to code assistance, selected 3D models and selected marketing artwork. Every area finding comes from the store disclosure text itself and rests on the developer&#39;s own statement, without an independent audit. No release date had been announced at review time.</p></details> </section> <section class="section" id="steam"> <div class="section-head"> <div><div class="eyebrow">STEAM DATA</div><h2>Steam data</h2></div> <div class="section-meta">Public data snapshot</div> </div> <div class="stat-grid"> <div class="stat"> <span>Online now</span> <strong>—</strong> <small>Steam public API</small> </div> <div class="stat"> <span>Steam reviews</span> <strong>—</strong> <small>No data</small> </div> <div class="stat"> <span>Positive reviews</span> <strong>—</strong> <small>All languages</small> </div> <div class="stat"> <span>Release date</span> <strong>—</strong> <small>To be announced（计划；核查时尚未发售）</small> </div> </div> <div class="steam-desc"><h3>Steam description</h3><p>挥舞炮管，用车身冲撞，突破AI的机械大军。这是一款主打华丽动作的单人坦克游戏——你摧毁得越多，AI的损失就越大。</p></div> <p class="source-line"> Player and review figures are Steam snapshots taken at build time and may be delayed. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/5186030/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View current data on Steam ↗</a> </p> </section> <section class="section" id="developer"> <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">DEVELOPER</div><h2>Developer</h2></div></div> <div class="dev-card"> <div class="dev-avatar">NE</div> <div class="dev-body"> <h3>Next Stage Inc.</h3> <p>Developer / publisher</p> <div class="dev-links"> <a href="https://nextstage.co.kr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Website ↗</a> <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/search/?developer=Next%20Stage%20Inc." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Developer on Steam ↗</a> <a href="https://github.com/COLDDCC/GameAIchecker/issues/new?title=SLAM%20TANK%EF%BC%885186030%EF%BC%89%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%E7%BA%A0%E9%94%99&body=%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%EF%BC%9Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fgameaichecker.com%2Fgames%2F5186030-slam-tank%2F%0A%0A%E9%9C%80%E8%A6%81%E7%BA%A0%E6%AD%A3%E7%9A%84%E5%86%85%E5%AE%B9%EF%BC%9A%0A%0A%E5%8E%9F%E5%A7%8B%E6%9D%A5%E6%BA%90%EF%BC%9A%0A%0A%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%9F%EF%BC%9A%0A" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claim / correct ↗</a> </div> </div> </div>  </section> <section class="section" id="community"> <div class="section-head"> <div><div class="eyebrow">COMMUNITY</div><h2>Player impressions</h2></div> <div class="section-meta">Separate from official disclosures</div> </div> <p class="section-lede">Player impressions are not evidence of AI use. Votes do not change developer disclosure findings.</p> <form id="voteForm" class="vote-form"> <select id="voteSelect" required aria-label="Choose your impression"> <option value="">Your impression…</option> <option value="no_ai_suspected">I suspect no AI use</option> <option value="some_ai_suspected">I suspect some AI use</option> <option value="heavy_ai_suspected">I suspect extensive AI use</option> <option value="all_ai_suspected">I suspect AI throughout</option> </select> <button class="btn primary" type="submit">Submit</button> </form> <p id="voteMessage" class="muted" role="status"></p> <div id="voteCounts" class="vote-counts"></div> <p class="source-line">Feedback availability does not affect the evidence. One vote per network per game.</p> </section> <section class="section" id="sources"> <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">SOURCES</div><h2>Sources &amp; review limits</h2></div></div> <ul class="source-list"> <li> <span>Official disclosure</span> <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/5186030/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Steam 商店完整 AI 披露</a> <time>2026-10-31</time> </li><li> <span>Steam discussion index</span> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Steam 讨论区首页核查</a> <time>2026-10-31</time> </li><li> <span>Community report</span> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/0/568174730608300015/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Everyone passing because AI</a> <time>2026-10-31</time> </li><li> <span>Community report</span> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/0/568175240219519653/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">People will be blown away in a year or two, when big AI projects will begin to release.</a> <time>2026-10-31</time> </li><li> <span>Community report</span> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/0/568175240219511182/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How are you gonna have an anti-AI plot and then use AI unironically?</a> <time>2026-10-31</time> </li><li> <span>Community report</span> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5186030/discussions/0/568174540165810821/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Was excited until i saw it was made by ai</a> <time>2026-10-31</time> </li> <li> <span>Steam store</span> <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/5186030/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SLAM TANK · App 5186030</a> <time></time> </li> </ul> <div class="callout"> <strong>Found an error?</strong> <p> Please include an original source, date and specific correction. <a href="https://github.com/COLDDCC/GameAIchecker/issues/new?title=SLAM%20TANK%EF%BC%885186030%EF%BC%89%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%E7%BA%A0%E9%94%99&body=%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%EF%BC%9Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fgameaichecker.com%2Fgames%2F5186030-slam-tank%2F%0A%0A%E9%9C%80%E8%A6%81%E7%BA%A0%E6%AD%A3%E7%9A%84%E5%86%85%E5%AE%B9%EF%BC%9A%0A%0A%E5%8E%9F%E5%A7%8B%E6%9D%A5%E6%BA%90%EF%BC%9A%0A%0A%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%9F%EF%BC%9A%0A" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Suggest a correction ↗</a> or <a href="https://github.com/COLDDCC/GameAIchecker/issues/new?title=SLAM%20TANK%20%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%E7%BA%A0%E9%94%99" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open a GitHub issue ↗</a>。
</p> </div> </section> <div class="share-bar"> <span>Share this game</span> <button class="btn" id="shareBtn2" type="button">Copy link</button> <a class="btn" href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=Does%20SLAM%20TANK%20use%20AI%3F&url=https%3A%2F%2Fgameaichecker.com%2Fgames%2F5186030-slam-tank%2F" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Share on X</a> <a class="btn" href="https://www.reddit.com/submit?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgameaichecker.com%2Fgames%2F5186030-slam-tank%2F&title=SLAM%20TANK%20%E2%80%94%20AI%20use%20evidence" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reddit</a> </div> </main> <div class="tf-cta-wrap"><a class="tf-cta" href="https://toolfavor.com/?utm_source=gameaichecker&utm_medium=footer_button" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3l1.9 4.6L18.5 9.5l-4.6 1.9L12 16l-1.9-4.6L5.5 9.5l4.6-1.9z"></path><path d="M19 15l.8 1.9 1.9.8-1.9.8L19 20.4l-.8-1.9-1.9-.8 1.9-.8z"></path></svg><span>Discover more useful tools on ToolFavor</span><svg class="tf-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></a></div> <footer class="site-footer"> <div class="wrap"> <span>Game AI Checker · Independent of Valve / Steam.</span> <span>Evidence first · Not stated does not mean unused</span> </div> </footer> <dialog class="lightbox" id="lightbox"> <button id="closeLightbox" type="button" aria-label="Close">×</button> <img id="lightboxImg" alt="" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high"> <div class="lightbox-caption" id="lightboxCaption"></div> </dialog> <script>
    (() => {
      const app = document.getElementById('app');
      const labels = JSON.parse(app?.dataset.ui || '{}');
      const tx = key => labels[key] || key;
      const en = document.documentElement.lang === 'en';
      const key = app?.dataset.gameKey || '';
      const slug = app?.dataset.slug || '';

      document.querySelectorAll('img[data-fallback]').forEach((img) => {
        const fallback = img.dataset.fallback;
        if (!fallback) return;
        img.addEventListener('error', function onError() {
          img.removeEventListener('error', onError);
          img.dataset.fallback = '';
          img.src = fallback;
          img.addEventListener('error', () => { img.style.display = 'none'; }, { once: true });
        });
      });

      const heroImg = document.getElementById('heroImg');
      const heroMedia = document.getElementById('heroMedia');
      const thumbs = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.thumb'));
      const counter = document.getElementById('mediaCount');
      const pauseBtn = document.getElementById('pauseBtn');
      let index = 0;
      let paused = false;
      let hovering = false;
      let timer = null;

      const warmedImages = new Set();
      function warm(full) {
        if (!full || warmedImages.has(full)) return null;
        warmedImages.add(full);
        const image = new Image();
        image.decoding = 'async';
        image.src = full;
        return image;
      }
      // Browse one frame ahead so the lightbox never waits on a cold round trip.
      function warmAround() {
        if (!thumbs.length) return;
        const upcoming = [thumbs[index], thumbs[(index + 1) % thumbs.length]];
        const run = () => upcoming.forEach((thumb) => thumb && warm(thumb.dataset.full));
        if (typeof window.requestIdleCallback === 'function') window.requestIdleCallback(run, { timeout: 1500 });
        else setTimeout(run, 500);
      }

      function show(next) {
        if (!heroImg || !thumbs.length) return;
        index = (next + thumbs.length) % thumbs.length;
        const thumb = thumbs[index];
        heroImg.src = thumb.dataset.src || heroImg.src;
        heroImg.dataset.full = thumb.dataset.full || heroImg.dataset.full;
        thumbs.forEach((item, position) => item.classList.toggle('active', position === index));
        if (counter) counter.textContent = `${index + 1} / ${thumbs.length}`;
        warmAround();
      }

      function schedule() {
        clearInterval(timer);
        if (thumbs.length < 2 || paused || hovering || document.hidden) return;
        timer = setInterval(() => show(index + 1), 6000);
      }

      thumbs.forEach((thumb) => {
        thumb.addEventListener('click', () => {
          show(Number(thumb.dataset.index || 0));
          schedule();
        });
      });

      document.getElementById('prevBtn')?.addEventListener('click', () => { show(index - 1); schedule(); });
      document.getElementById('nextBtn')?.addEventListener('click', () => { show(index + 1); schedule(); });
      pauseBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        paused = !paused;
        pauseBtn.textContent = paused ? '▶' : 'Ⅱ';
        pauseBtn.setAttribute('aria-label', paused ? tx("继续轮播") : tx("暂停轮播"));
        schedule();
      });
      heroMedia?.addEventListener('mouseenter', () => { hovering = true; schedule(); });
      heroMedia?.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => { hovering = false; schedule(); });
      document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', schedule);
      schedule();

      const appId = app?.dataset.appid;
      if (appId && heroImg && !heroImg.getAttribute('src')?.startsWith('/images/steam/')) {
        fetch(`/api/steam-media?id=${encodeURIComponent(appId)}`)
          .then((response) => (response.ok ? response.json() : Promise.reject()))
          .then((data) => {
            if (!data?.available) return;
            for (const shot of data.screenshots || []) {
              const src = shot.thumbnail || shot.full;
              const full = shot.full || shot.thumbnail;
              if (!src || thumbs.some((thumb) => thumb.dataset.full === full)) continue;
              const thumb = document.createElement('button');
              thumb.className = 'thumb';
              thumb.type = 'button';
              thumb.dataset.src = src;
              thumb.dataset.full = full;
              thumb.dataset.index = String(thumbs.length);
              thumb.setAttribute('aria-label', `第 ${thumbs.length + 1} 张图片`);
              const image = document.createElement('img');
              image.src = src;
              image.alt = '';
              image.loading = 'lazy';
              image.decoding = 'async';
              thumb.append(image);
              thumb.addEventListener('click', () => { show(Number(thumb.dataset.index)); schedule(); });
              document.getElementById('thumbs')?.append(thumb);
              thumbs.push(thumb);
            }
            if (counter) counter.textContent = `${index + 1} / ${thumbs.length}`;
            const countText = document.getElementById('mediaCountText');
            if (countText) countText.textContent = `${thumbs.length} ${en ? 'official images' : '张官方图片'}`;
            schedule();

            if (data.movies?.length) {
              const mediaCol = document.querySelector('.media-col');
              let videos = document.querySelector('.videos');
              if (!videos && mediaCol) {
                videos = document.createElement('div');
                videos.className = 'videos';
                videos.innerHTML = '<div class="mini-title"></div><div class="video-grid"></div>';
                videos.querySelector('.mini-title').textContent = tx('宣传视频');
                mediaCol.append(videos);
              }
              const grid = videos?.querySelector('.video-grid');
              if (grid) {
                const first = data.movies.find((movie) => movie.webm || movie.mp4);
                if (first) {
                  const player = document.createElement('video');
                  player.className = 'trailer';
                  player.controls = true;
                  player.preload = 'none';
                  player.poster = first.thumbnail || '';
                  player.src = first.webm || first.mp4;
                  grid.before(player);
                }
                for (const movie of data.movies.slice(0, 4)) {
                  if (!movie.thumbnail) continue;
                  const link = document.createElement('a');
                  link.className = 'video-card';
                  link.href = data.steamUrl || `https://store.steampowered.com/app/${appId}/`;
                  link.target = '_blank';
                  link.rel = 'noopener noreferrer';
                  const poster = document.createElement('img');
                  poster.src = movie.thumbnail;
                  poster.alt = movie.name || tx("宣传视频");
                  poster.loading = 'lazy';
                  const label = document.createElement('span');
                  label.textContent = `${movie.name || tx("观看宣传视频")} ↗`;
                  link.append(poster, label);
                  grid.append(link);
                }
              }
            }
          })
          .catch(() => {});
      }

      const lightbox = document.getElementById('lightbox');
      const lightboxImg = document.getElementById('lightboxImg');
      const lightboxCaption = document.getElementById('lightboxCaption');
      function openLightbox() {
        if (!heroImg || !lightbox || !lightboxImg) return;
        const full = heroImg.dataset.full || heroImg.src;
        // The 1280 hero frame is already decoded, so the dialog shows at once and upgrades in place.
        lightboxImg.src = heroImg.currentSrc || heroImg.src;
        lightboxImg.alt = heroImg.alt || '';
        if (lightboxCaption) lightboxCaption.textContent = heroImg.alt || '';
        if (typeof lightbox.showModal === 'function') lightbox.showModal();
        const larger = warm(full);
        if (larger) larger.onload = () => { lightboxImg.src = larger.src; };
      }
      document.getElementById('openLightbox')?.addEventListener('click', openLightbox);
      heroImg?.addEventListener('click', openLightbox);
      [document.getElementById('openLightbox'), heroMedia].forEach((node) => node?.addEventListener('pointerenter', () => warm(heroImg?.dataset.full), { once: true }));
      document.getElementById('closeLightbox')?.addEventListener('click', () => lightbox?.close());
      lightbox?.addEventListener('click', (event) => { if (event.target === lightbox) lightbox.close(); });

      const saveBtn = document.getElementById('saveBtn');
      const starKey = `gac:star:${slug}`;
      function paintStar() {
        if (!saveBtn) return;
        const active = localStorage.getItem(starKey) === '1';
        saveBtn.textContent = active ? tx("★ 已收藏") : tx("☆ 收藏");
        saveBtn.classList.toggle('active', active);
      }
      saveBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (localStorage.getItem(starKey) === '1') localStorage.removeItem(starKey);
        else localStorage.setItem(starKey, '1');
        paintStar();
      });
      paintStar();

      async function copyLink() {
        const url = window.location.href;
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(url);
          flash(tx("链接已复制"));
        } catch {
          window.prompt(tx("复制链接"), url);
        }
      }
      function flash(message) {
        const target = document.getElementById('voteMessage') || document.getElementById('shareBtn');
        if (!target) return;
        const original = target.textContent;
        if (target.id === 'voteMessage') {
          target.textContent = message;
          setTimeout(() => { target.textContent = original; }, 2200);
        } else {
          target.textContent = message;
          setTimeout(() => { target.textContent = tx("分享"); }, 2200);
        }
      }
      async function share() {
        if (navigator.share) {
          try {
            await navigator.share({ title: document.title, url: window.location.href });
            return;
          } catch {}
        }
        copyLink();
      }
      document.getElementById('shareBtn')?.addEventListener('click', share);
      document.getElementById('shareBtn2')?.addEventListener('click', copyLink);

      document.getElementById('copyId')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const id = app?.dataset.appid;
        if (!id) return;
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(id);
          flash(tx("App ID 已复制"));
        } catch {}
      });

      const voteForm = document.getElementById('voteForm');
      const voteMessage = document.getElementById('voteMessage');
      const voteCounts = document.getElementById('voteCounts');
      const voteSelect = document.getElementById('voteSelect');
      const voteNames = {
        no_ai_suspected: tx("认为没有使用 AI"),
        some_ai_suspected: tx("认为部分使用 AI"),
        heavy_ai_suspected: tx("认为大量使用 AI"),
        all_ai_suspected: tx("认为几乎全程使用 AI"),
      };
      function showCounts(counts) {
        if (!voteCounts) return;
        voteCounts.replaceChildren();
        for (const [code, label] of Object.entries(voteNames)) {
          const value = Number(counts?.[code] || 0);
          if (!value) continue;
          const row = document.createElement('div');
          row.textContent = en ? `${value} players ${label}` : `${value} 位玩家${label}`;
          voteCounts.append(row);
        }
      }
      if (voteForm && key) {
        fetch(`/api/feedback?game=${encodeURIComponent(key)}`)
          .then((response) => (response.ok ? response.json() : Promise.reject()))
          .then((data) => {
            showCounts(data.counts);
            if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = tx("反馈功能已启用。");
          })
          .catch(() => {
            if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = tx("匿名反馈暂未启用，等待管理员配置数据库。");
          });
        voteForm.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
          event.preventDefault();
          const vote = voteSelect?.value;
          if (!vote) return;
          const button = voteForm.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
          if (button) button.disabled = true;
          try {
            const response = await fetch('/api/feedback', {
              method: 'POST',
              headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
              body: JSON.stringify({ game: key, vote }),
            });
            const data = await response.json();
            if (!response.ok) {
              if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = response.status === 409 ? tx("该网络已对本游戏投过票。") : tx("提交失败，请稍后再试。");
              if (data.counts) showCounts(data.counts);
            } else {
              if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = tx("反馈已记录，谢谢参与。");
              showCounts(data.counts);
              voteForm.reset();
            }
          } catch {
            if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = tx("网络错误，请稍后重试。");
          } finally {
            if (button) button.disabled = false;
          }
        });
      }

      const navLinks = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.section-nav a'));
      if (navLinks.length && 'IntersectionObserver' in window) {
        const linksById = new Map(navLinks.map((link) => [link.getAttribute('href')?.slice(1), link]));
        const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          for (const entry of entries) {
            if (!entry.isIntersecting) continue;
            navLinks.forEach((link) => link.classList.remove('active'));
            linksById.get(entry.target.id)?.classList.add('active');
          }
        }, { rootMargin: '-35% 0px -55% 0px' });
        document.querySelectorAll('section[id]').forEach((section) => observer.observe(section));
      }
    })();
  </script> <script>
    document.getElementById('game-language')?.addEventListener('change', (event) => {
      const slug = document.getElementById('app')?.dataset.slug;
      if (slug) window.location.assign('/games/' + (event.target.value === 'en' ? '' : event.target.value + '/') + encodeURIComponent(slug) + '/' + location.hash);
    });
  </script> </body> </html>